    "Does screening actually save lives? Yes, shown in randomised trials rather than inferred. Three annual low-dose CT scans cut lung cancer deaths by 20.0 percent in 53,454 Americans (National Lung Screening Trial 2011), and four rounds of volume CT cut them by 24 percent in Dutch and Belgian men at ten years (NELSON 2020). It takes 323 people screened over 6.5 years, or 130 over ten years, to prevent one lung cancer death.",
